# Everything the image must not contain.
#
# The first entries are the ones that matter. A .env copied into an image is a
# credential published with it: image layers are readable by anyone who can pull
# the image, and deleting the file in a later layer does not remove it from the
# earlier one. `docker history` is enough to recover it.
#
# There is a test for this in the repository (tests/test_no_secrets_committed.py)
# but it guards *git*, not Docker. This file is the equivalent guard for images,
# and it is deny-by-accident rather than deny-by-default — so it is worth reading
# rather than skimming.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Version control and CI
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local environments and caches
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Model cache — deliberately excluded so it is fetched during the build on the
# target platform rather than copied from a developer machine, where it may be
# a different architecture.
.fastembed_cache
.index

# Not needed at runtime. Tests are run by CI, not by the container.
tests
eval/results
docs
*.md
!README.md
